invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: table_select never adds the high half of an entry's Y into its
  sum, so every entry it returns has Y's two high limbs zero and the base
  multiplication adds a point off the curve in every window.
  bin/p256_equiv_test holds the base multiplication to p256_point_base_mul,
  and proof/p256_wide_digit_harness.c proves the scan returns the entry at
  every index, limb for limb.

--- old
        y_high |= entry_y_high & masks;
--- new
        (void)entry_y_high;
